  "details": "We need a MASSIVE IMPROVEMENT in the \"look at me' feature in the vrchat camera. \n\nThe focal point in the \"look at me\" is \"FIXED\" it looks at somewhere in the middle of your body, and i want it to be \"FLEXIBLE\" , so let's say i stick my hand in front of the camera, and i say \"look at me\" i want my hand and not my body to be the focus, and the camera to be able to go 360 degree around my hand. I don't want those other already existing functions to do any job like this, i want a new function for this. One that actually works, so that if you put your feet in the camera, and press \"look at me\" it will actually have the feet as the focus point. Basically i'm saying, please make the focus point flexible with the 'look at me' function. As a streamer, i have been bothered by the lack of this functionality since the beginning, i should've made a post about this much earlier.",
